<title>HONG KONG: HK May provisional trade deficit HK$17.5 bln.</title>
<headline>HK May provisional trade deficit HK$17.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department released the following data showing a provisional visible trade deficit of HK$17.5 billion in May (rounded figures in billions of H.K. dollars):</p>
<p>			    May '97	Apr '97	 May '96</p>
<p> Trade balance	  -17.5	  -18.11	  -12.02</p>
<p> Domestic Exports	16.8	   16.46	   17.62</p>
<p> Re-exports	     100.2	  104.53	  100.29</p>
<p> Total exports	  117.0	  121.99	  117.91</p>
<p> Imports		  134.5	  139.10	  129.92</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for year ended:</p>
<p>			   May '97	 Apr '97	  May '96</p>
<p> Trade balance	 -152.73	 -147.23	  -142.05</p>
<p> Domestic exports     207.76	  208.55	   226.53</p>
<p> Re-exports	   1,200.82	1,200.94	 1,150.15</p>
<p> Total exports	1,408.58	1,409.49	 1,376.68</p>
<p> Imports		1,561.31	1,556.73	 1,518.73</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
